   "description": "How the system auto-picks a configuration when both an ISIC hierarchy and an Address Division hierarchy apply:<ul><li><b>Address-First (Regional Priority):</b> the most specific division wins; ISIC walk breaks ties within a division.</li><li><b>ISIC-First (Configuration Priority):</b> resolve the default Service Configuration by the ISIC walk first, then override only with a Regional Service Configuration that references it.</li><li><b>Most Specific Overall:</b> pick the candidate with the smallest combined (ISIC + division) distance; a regional match wins ties.</li></ul>",
